From a0a6054e0bf2c9316a31039b998741b10080a695 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patch <patch@local>
Date: Tue, 26 May 2026 21:49:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Vendor libwifi (parse-only subset) + xtensa-newlib port
 shims

Adds libwifi from https://github.com/libwifi/libwifi at the parse-only
subset under esp32/lib/libwifi/ (the gen/ tree is omitted; this firmware
only consumes promiscuous captures, never generates 802.11 frames).

Port shims under esp32/lib/libwifi-port/ provide endian.h and byteswap.h
for xtensa-esp32-elf newlib, which does not ship these. The shims use
__builtin_bswap intrinsics. Big-endian is treated as untested-on-ESP32
(ESP32 LX6 is LE).

One single-line change in libwifi/core/misc/byteswap.h converts an
include from quoted to angled form ("byteswap.h" -> <byteswap.h>) so
the port shim wins instead of infinite-including libwifi's own header.
